<title>BELGIUM: Electrabel 1996 net profit up 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Electrabel 1996 net profit up 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)		352		 vs    339</p>
<p>    Group net profit	    30.398		 vs 28.812</p>
<p>NOTE - Utility holding company Electrabel, controlled by Tractebel through its Powerfin unit, said turnover in electricity rose 0.9 percent to 117.606 billion francs, and it had implemented a second phase of price cutting in January. Turnover in natural gas for public distribution rose 14.5 percent to 29.720 billion francs, it said, noting that 1996 was on average much colder than 1995.</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	     30.413	     vs 28.829</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	 38.212	     vs 35.345</p>
<p>    Net current profit	  29.782	     vs 28.548</p>
<p>    Tax charges		    8.430	     vs  6.797</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		221.485	     vs 215.956</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	    631			281</p>
<p>Dividend payment date: May 28, 1997</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
